  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466296",
      "title": "Building a Custom Observable",
      "lectureOrder": 498,
      "videoOrder": 457,
      "sourceHash": "76cd33a80469ef1057165a7bebf570ebefb03ac795f3a22e638a200d1f9b88b6",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.19,
          "end": 4.71,
          "en": "Speaker 1: So I promised you a custom observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.71,
          "end": 6.18,
          "en": "to understand its internals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.18,
          "end": 8.04,
          "en": "and what I gave you was interval.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.04,
          "end": 10.2,
          "en": "Now it's closer to a custom observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.2,
          "end": 13.069,
          "en": "because it's not coming from some Angular feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.069,
          "end": 16.38,
          "en": "but still this of course is kind of a utility function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.38,
          "end": 18.298,
          "en": "that gives us a predefined observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.298,
          "end": 20.931,
          "en": "that fires a number every second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.931,
          "end": 25.26,
          "en": "Well actually we can rebuild this manually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.26,
          "end": 26.61,
          "en": "Let's comment out this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.61,
          "end": 30.09,
          "en": "and let's build a real custom observable now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.09,
          "end": 33.12,
          "en": "I'll store that in an observable, in a constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.12,
          "end": 35.24,
          "en": "and I'll name it customObservable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.24,
          "end": 39.069,
          "en": "or customIntervalObservable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.069,
          "end": 41.25,
          "en": "You can of course pick any name you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.25,
          "end": 43.32,
          "en": "And to create a new observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.32,
          "end": 47.22,
          "en": "we can simply import Observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.22,
          "end": 49.623,
          "en": "the type itself, from rxjs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.46,
          "end": 52.26,
          "en": "Now you can use observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.26,
          "end": 54.51,
          "en": "and call a create method on that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 54.51,
          "end": 55.95,
          "en": "And this will do what it sounds like,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 55.95,
          "end": 57.573,
          "en": "it creates a new observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 58.41,
          "end": 61.35,
          "en": "Now, create actually takes a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 61.35,
          "end": 64.189,
          "en": "and I'll pass in an anonymous arrow function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 64.189,
          "end": 68.52,
          "en": "like this, which will get an argument automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 68.52,
          "end": 71.1,
          "en": "Rxjs will pass in that argument for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 71.1,
          "end": 73.89,
          "en": "And that argument is a so-called observer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 73.89,
          "end": 75.87,
          "en": "Now what's an observer?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 75.87,
          "end": 77.7,
          "en": "Now you heard about the observer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 77.7,
          "end": 79.53,
          "en": "in the first video of this module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 79.53,
          "end": 84.06,
          "en": "The observer in the end is the part that is interested",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 84.06,
          "end": 86.31,
          "en": "in being informed about new data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 86.31,
          "end": 90.39,
          "en": "about errors, or about the observable being completed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 90.39,
          "end": 94.86,
          "en": "Now our job here is to tell the observer about new data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 94.86,
          "end": 98.67,
          "en": "about an error, or about the observable being completed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 98.67,
          "end": 100.8,
          "en": "Here, we're not responsible for listening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 100.8,
          "end": 102.69,
          "en": "because the observer is the listener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 102.69,
          "end": 105.99000000000001,
          "en": "Here, we get that listening part as an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 105.99000000000001,
          "end": 108.69,
          "en": "and we need to tell it once we're done,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 108.69,
          "end": 110.97,
          "en": "once new data is there, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 110.97,
          "end": 112.65,
          "en": "So in this anonymous function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 112.65,
          "end": 116.7,
          "en": "we can now use the regular set interval method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 116.7,
          "end": 118.74000000000001,
          "en": "and, uh, set an interval of one second,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 118.74000000000001,
          "end": 120.33,
          "en": "let's say, as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 120.33,
          "end": 122.43,
          "en": "Now this again receives an anonymous function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 122.43,
          "end": 124.14,
          "en": "It's the normal set interval method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 124.14,
          "end": 126,
          "en": "nothing special about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 126,
          "end": 127.617,
          "en": "An insight of said interval here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 127.617,
          "end": 132.39,
          "en": "We can now call console log, or do whatever we want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 132.39,
          "end": 134.19,
          "en": "or simply use our observer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 134.19,
          "end": 137.67000000000002,
          "en": "And there we now got methods like next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 137.67000000000002,
          "end": 141.45,
          "en": "We can call next here to emit a new value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 141.45,
          "end": 142.56,
          "en": "and that is important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 142.56,
          "end": 145.05,
          "en": "The observer has a couple of important methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 145.05,
          "end": 146.67000000000002,
          "en": "Next is one of them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 146.67000000000002,
          "end": 148.35,
          "en": "error is another of them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 148.35,
          "end": 151.05,
          "en": "so that would be the one you use to throw an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 151.05,
          "end": 153.27,
          "en": "and complete is one to let the observer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 153.27,
          "end": 154.47,
          "en": "know that you're done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 154.47,
          "end": 156.78,
          "en": "Here, however we use next,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 156.78,
          "end": 159.632,
          "en": "and to also have an incrementing number here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 159.632,
          "end": 163.02,
          "en": "we can simply introduce a variable count,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 163.02,
          "end": 164.493,
          "en": "which starts at zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 166.59,
          "end": 168.81,
          "en": "Inside of our setInterval,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 168.81,
          "end": 170.89,
          "en": "we then simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 173.16,
          "end": 174.93,
          "en": "pass this on to next",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 174.93,
          "end": 178.47,
          "en": "and we then increment count by one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 178.47,
          "end": 180.03,
          "en": "So now here our count starts at zero,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 180.03,
          "end": 182.73,
          "en": "we incremented by one whenever it setInterval fires,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 182.73,
          "end": 185.493,
          "en": "and we let our observer know about that new data here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 186.93,
          "end": 190.38,
          "en": "Now we can also subscribe to our custom observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 190.38,
          "end": 193.14,
          "en": "and I'll do this in the same place here, in ngOnInit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 193.14,
          "end": 195.24,
          "en": "Of course, you could do this in other places too",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 195.24,
          "end": 197.16,
          "en": "if this were stored in a service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 197.16,
          "end": 199.8,
          "en": "or in a property of that component simply.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 199.8,
          "end": 202.53300000000002,
          "en": "So here, I can now call subscribe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 203.55,
          "end": 206.49,
          "en": "and to subscribe you pass the same thing as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 206.49,
          "end": 209.825,
          "en": "a function that simply accepts the data we're emitting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 209.825,
          "end": 212.13,
          "en": "So in this case we could name it \"count again\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 212.13,
          "end": 213.63,
          "en": "or, to avoid naming confusion,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 213.63,
          "end": 215.185,
          "en": "simply name it \"data\", whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 215.185,
          "end": 219.70499999999998,
          "en": "And here I will now console-log that data, just as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 219.70499999999998,
          "end": 222.15,
          "en": "Now, let's save that all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 222.15,
          "end": 224.43,
          "en": "and let's wait for this page to reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 224.43,
          "end": 226.8,
          "en": "And again, you see the same result as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 226.8,
          "end": 229.56,
          "en": "but now we built our own interval observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 229.56,
          "end": 232.74,
          "en": "And this is roughly what's happening under the hood here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 232.74,
          "end": 234.972,
          "en": "for the built-in interval observable too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 234.972,
          "end": 239.67000000000002,
          "en": "It's giving us an observable, which will essentially fire",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 239.67000000000002,
          "end": 242.94,
          "en": "um, for every X-milliseconds we defined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 242.94,
          "end": 245.73,
          "en": "and it lets our observer know about that new data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 245.73,
          "end": 247.47,
          "en": "That's what's happening here too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 247.47,
          "end": 250.98,
          "en": "And if I navigate away, well then we get a problem here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 250.98,
          "end": 253.83,
          "en": "because I try to call unsubscribe of undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 253.83,
          "end": 255.51,
          "en": "because I don't store my subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 255.51,
          "end": 257.4,
          "en": "Of course, that should be done here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 257.4,
          "end": 260.01,
          "en": "So in my first Obs subscription,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 260.01,
          "end": 262.44,
          "en": "I'll now store that subscription again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 262.44,
          "end": 264.78,
          "en": "simply by storing the result of subscribe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 264.78,
          "end": 266.16,
          "en": "and the subscription again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 266.16,
          "end": 267.93,
          "en": "So now with that, that reloads",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 267.93,
          "end": 270.33,
          "en": "and I navigate away that works without issues.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 270.33,
          "end": 273.65999999999997,
          "en": "Again, if I go back, a new observable starts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 273.65999999999997,
          "end": 277.144,
          "en": "So this is working and this is a real custom observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 277.144,
          "end": 279.81,
          "en": "and this shows us how to emit new data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 279.81,
          "end": 282.87,
          "en": "But what about errors and completing the observable?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 282.87,
          "end": 284.283,
          "en": "I mentioned this as well.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
